The OS is irrelevant in this case.
It depends on whether or not the dump patch is installed.
And if it is, whether or not some valid dump file name is configured.

If you downloaded the game binaries from the official devteam site, you
don't have the dump patch.
If you downloaded binaries from somewhere else, it depends.. and the site
should mention it if there are patches included.
If you compiled the game yourself, you probably would know and wouldn't
be asking..

The #version command may or may not show which patches are included, but
the most reliable way to verify this is probaly the O command.
Check the "compounds" section of the options. If it includes "dumpfile"
option, the patch is installed.

